From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 16:36:10 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq-phanbell: describe the pcie0 monitor
 clocks

WIP for problem 2: replace the anatop register writes in 0033 with an
assigned-clocks description.

The previous attempt at this was reverted because it produced the right
hardware state and pcie0 still would not link. It listed only the two
monitor clocks in assigned-clocks, and a property set in a &label
override replaces the whole property, so it deleted the pcie1_ctrl,
pcie1_phy and pcie1_aux parents and rates that imx8mq.dtsi sets for
every i.MX8MQ board. The evidence gathered at the time cannot rule that
out: clk_summary was only ever read for the monitor subtree, which was
configured correctly both times.

List all five so nothing is dropped. The mux value the clk framework
ends up writing is the same 0xb that 0033 writes, since
sys_pll1_out_monitor is index 11 in pllout_monitor_sels.

Not folded into 0011 yet, and 0033 is still in place, so this changes
nothing on its own beyond making the assignments explicit.
---
 .../boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts    | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
index ef1e43c322f4..5b505fe297d9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
@@ -868,3 +868,29 @@ &mhdp {
 &dcss {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
+
+/*
+ * WIP for problem 2. A property set in a &label override replaces the whole
+ * property rather than adding to it, so the monitor clocks have to be listed
+ * alongside the three assignments imx8mq.dtsi already makes for pcie0. The
+ * earlier attempt at this listed only the monitor clocks, which silently
+ * dropped the pcie1_ctrl, pcie1_phy and pcie1_aux parents and rates - and
+ * nobody noticed, because clk_summary was only ever read for the monitor
+ * subtree, which was configured correctly.
+ *
+ * Test in two steps: build with 0033 still in place and confirm nothing
+ * regresses, then delete 0033 and see whether pcie0 still links.
+ */
+&pcie0 {
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_PCIE1_CTRL>,
+			  <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_PCIE1_PHY>,
+			  <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_PCIE1_AUX>,
+			  <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_MON_SEL>,
+			  <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_MON_SYS_PLL1_DIV>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk IMX8MQ_SYS2_PLL_250M>,
+				 <&clk IMX8MQ_SYS2_PLL_100M>,
+				 <&clk IMX8MQ_SYS1_PLL_80M>,
+				 <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_MON_SYS_PLL1_DIV>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <250000000>, <100000000>, <10000000>,
+			       <0>, <100000000>;
+};
